# Accepted vulnerabilities, with justification and an expiry.
# Reviewed: 2026-09-13    Next review: 2026-12-13
#
# Policy: HIGH and CRITICAL findings fail the pipeline, and ignore-unfixed is
# on — so only findings with a released fix can break the build. A finding is
# accepted here only when both hold: there is no released fix, and the
# vulnerable code path is not reachable in this service.
#
# Apache Tomcat: 10.1.55 is the latest release in the 10.1.x line; the fix
# versions quoted below (10.1.58, 11.0.25) are not published yet. All three
# findings concern authentication and security-constraint mechanisms corepay
# does not use. Authentication is stateless JWT bearer tokens validated by
# Spring Security's OAuth2 resource server; the DIGEST and FORM authenticators
# are never configured, and there is no web.xml declaring security
# constraints — authorisation is expressed entirely in SecurityConfig.
# Action: bump tomcat.version as soon as 10.1.58 ships, then delete this file.
CVE-2026-65182
